    "created_at": "2024-01-15T08:20:09Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-01-15T08:20:09Z",
    "body": "> I think the bug here is a bit more subtle. It should not be possible to set init[\"baseURL\"] to null because its type is USVString, not USVString?. But I guess the spec does that in \"initialize\" step 2.3.\r\n\r\nI overlooked the type. Yes, it's `USVString` so it can't be null. Thanks.\r\n\r\nHow about adding an empty string guard to between step 2.2 and 2.3 and throwing a TypeError?",
